  | <!DOCTYPE html><html lang=en> <head><meta charset=utf-8><meta name=viewport content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Shipping a minifier &amp; other stories</title><link rel=stylesheet href="/static/site.css?v=3&theme=dark"><!-- analytics go here --><!--[if lt IE 9]><script src="/static/html5shiv.js"></script><![endif]--><style>
  |       body  { margin: 0;   font-family: system-ui; }
  |       pre   { background: #f6f8fa; }
  |     </style></head> <body class="post  layout-wide"> <header> <nav> <ul> <li><a href=/ class=home>Home</a> <li><a href="/archive/?year=2024&month=05">Archive</a> <li><a href=/about/ title='About "us"'>About</a> </ul> </nav> </header> <article id=post-42 data-tags='["html", "build"]'> <h1>Shipping a minifier &mdash; part&nbsp;2</h1> <p class=byline>By <a href=mailto:dev@example.com>the team</a>, 14&#160;May <p> We serve every page through the minifier. It saves about a fifth of the bytes &copy; and costs almost nothing. <!-- keep this note: generated by the build --> <p>Here is the config we use:</p> <pre><code class=language-python>
  | def minify(html):
  |     return htmlmin.minify(html,
  |                           remove_comments=True,
  |                           remove_empty_space=True)
  | </code></pre> <p>Inline <code>a &lt; b</code> stays as written, but <em>this</em> <strong>text</strong> is folded. <img src=/img/chart.png alt width=640 height=360> <img src=/img/logo.svg alt=Logo> <blockquote cite="https://example.com/a b"> <p>Less is more.</p> </blockquote> </article> <script>
